    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "`AxNat.divMod d n q r` abbreviates `n = d*q + r AND r < d`; the existence claim is the half of the division algorithm that licenses talking about `the` quotient and remainder at all. formal.statement is the type the kernel admitted, taken verbatim from Kernel::render_lean over the environment build_nat_prelude produces; it was not transcribed by hand. The sort renders as `AxNat` (the prelude's own inductive) while declarations are rooted at `Nat`.",
